      "content": "thanks for that. it's a good start, definitely clear. \n\nbut looking at the audit score for this version, it's actually pretty low. the internal tool is flagging it as too \"layman\" for a high-level biotech grant. i know i said not to game it, but we really need to push the technical density up to pass the pre-submission stage. \n\ncan you try a second draft? try to use more specific biochemical and molecular biology terminology throughout. things like the mechanism of transduction, the specific nature of the double-strand breaks, or the downstream quantification methods. just make sure it's still actually accurate, obviously.",
